
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
homolyze  fsplit ⋈ tensor_product_operation — the radical-generating reverse of click
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  the fsplit—tensor_product_operation σ-bond: a click on R↔S (Δ=2.00) — a shared electron pair, the reaction center.
  → homolysis splits that pair EVENLY (δ_A): each fragment keeps ONE electron — the SOMO:
      fsplit•  ⟨𐑼𐑰𐑩𐑹𐑐𐑧𐑲𐑜⊙𐑓𐑳𐑷⟩   neutral radical — SOMO open on R↔S, seeks a partner  [⊡=𐑷 even — SOMO is the opened bond center]
      tensor_product_operation•  ⟨𐑛𐑥𐑾𐑿𐑱𐑤𐑚𐑠𐑢𐑖𐑙𐑷⟩   neutral radical — SOMO open on R↔S  [⊡=𐑷 even — SOMO is the opened bond center]
  recombination (μ): fsplit• + tensor_product_operation• → fsplit—tensor_product_operation  — radical coupling re-pairs the SOMO (μ∘δ=id, lossless).
  heterolytic alternative (δ_D → ion pair): the same bond can break UNEVENLY — one fragment takes both
    electrons (anion), the other none (cation): the single-electron / radical-ion route — `./ask --set fsplit tensor_product_operation` → fsplit•⁺ / tensor_product_operation•⁻.
